 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Reporting what someone else said",
     "texto": [
      "Vietnamese doesn't conjugate the verb to agree with the tense of the introductory clause. **Rằng** or **là** can introduce what was said: «Lan nói: “Tôi bận.”» → «Lan nói là cô ấy bận» = Lan said that she was busy.",
      "When you report it, adjust the references to the new context: «tôi» can change to **cô ấy/anh ấy**; time or place words can also change. If you reproduce the exact words, keep the direct quote.",
      "**Là** is very common in speech; **rằng** is seen more in written or formal registers. Sometimes they're omitted, but not in every construction. Your choice of pronouns depends on the relationship between the people.",
      "Useful verbs: **nói** (to say), **bảo** (to tell/ask someone to do something), **kể** (to tell), **cho biết** (to inform), **trả lời** (to answer), **khen** (to praise), **chê** (to criticise)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Reporting a question or an order",
     "texto": [
      "A yes-or-no question: **hỏi (xem)… có… không**: «Anh ấy hỏi tôi **có** thích phim đó **không**» = He asked me whether I liked that film.",
      "With a question word, it stays the same: «Cô ấy hỏi tôi **mấy giờ** phim bắt đầu» = She asked me what time the film starts.",
      "An order or request: **bảo / nhờ / khuyên + person + verb**: «Mẹ **bảo** tôi về sớm» = My mum told me to come home early."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
